# Discovery Changelog

**Date:** 2026-08-30
**Mode:** Brownfield (post-MVP ideation)
**Previous Version:** 1.1

## What Changed

| Document | Section | Change Type | Summary |
|----------|---------|-------------|---------|
| product-vision.md | 9. Design Direction | Modified | Replaced the neutral/calm color palette bullet with adoption of the PeakFlames Design System (dark-first obsidian canvas, flame accent, Archivo/IBM Plex Sans/JetBrains Mono); bridged "avoid aggressive notification-style UI" to the system's "one hot element per view" rule. |
| product-vision.md | 11. Backlog / Future Vision | Modified | Removed "Dark mode / theme toggle" (dark is now the default, not a future feature); replaced with "Light theme toggle" since the system ships a `[data-theme="light"]` scope. |

## New Capabilities Identified

- Adoption of the PeakFlames Design System as Summit's visual language — dark-first theming,
  brand type ramp, flame/ember accent treatment, and the "one hot element per view" restraint
  rule, applied across the existing habit list, filter, and empty-state UI without any DOM or
  copy changes.

## Priority Signal

This is purely a visual restyle of existing, already-implemented behavior — no new user-facing
functionality. Priority is to make Summit visibly a PeakFlames product while preserving every
existing behavioral TOR (streak prominence, done-state distinction, filter selection,
responsive layout at 375px/1280px) exactly as specified.

## Deferred Items

- Light theme toggle UI (backlog item, not part of this cycle — dark ships as the sole default).
- The design system's React components, UI kits, guidelines, and brand assets (favicon) —
  vanilla-TS Summit only vendors the token CSS layer.
